{"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/mixpanelencoding"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"abstract":[{"text":"Send records to a Mixpanel project through its track API.","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/mixpanel(projectToken:region:plan:backoff:clock:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" makes an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" (module "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":") for your Mixpanel project in one call. It checks"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the project token, posts to the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\/track"},{"type":"text","text":" endpoint of the project’s data residency"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelRegion","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":") with a "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelBatchEncoder","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", and splits each batch to Mixpanel’s limits"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelBatchEncoder\/batchLimit","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"): 2,000 events and 2 MB a request. A batch with no record the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"encoder can write, an empty one included, makes no request. It retries no response, a 5xx, 408"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and 429, and drops and reports any other status. The token goes in each event, so no header field"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is needed, and no trace context is sent. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import Traffluent"},{"type":"text","text":" leaves this module out; import it on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"its own."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The project token is public: Mixpanel’s own apps and web pages ship it. The destination takes","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"nothing else. Never put the project’s secret or a service account’s credentials in an app; they","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"belong to Mixpanel’s import API, for servers. The factory throws ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelSetupError","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" for an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"empty token, and for one with a character other than a letter or digit, which no project token","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"has.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The region has no default. A project’s data resides in the US, the EU or India, and Mixpanel","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"ingests nothing for it from another residency’s endpoint, so you pick the region on purpose.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each record becomes an event of an anonymous user. Its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"distinct_id"},{"type":"text","text":" is the record’s session,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"from the sessions enricher, also sent as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$device_id"},{"type":"text","text":"; a record with no session is sent under its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"own record identifier, with no "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$device_id"},{"type":"text","text":". Under Simplified ID Merge, Mixpanel shows a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"session’s events under "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$device:<session>"},{"type":"text","text":", and a sessionless record’s under its bare record"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"identifier. No "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$user_id"},{"type":"text","text":" is sent. Its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$insert_id"},{"type":"text","text":" is the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"record’s identifier, which a redelivered record keeps, and its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"time"},{"type":"text","text":" the record’s timestamp in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"epoch milliseconds. The record’s vendor identifier and trace context aren’t sent. Each event’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ip"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0"},{"type":"text","text":", as is the endpoint’s, so Mixpanel adds no location from the request’s address. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"standard context is sent as Mixpanel’s default properties ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$app_version_string"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$app_build_number"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$model"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$wifi"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$os"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$os_version"},{"type":"text","text":")."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Mixpanel counts a user per "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"distinct_id"},{"type":"text","text":", so each session is one user in its reports, and so is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"each record sent without a session. On a Mixpanel plan billed by monthly tracked users, each counts"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"as one."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Properties are read through the event’s schema in the ","type":"text"},{"code":"TrackingPlan","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" the encoder is made with. A","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"Sensitive","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" value is never sent, whatever the record reveals. A record the encoder can’t write is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"left out and the rest of the batch is sent: one the plan doesn’t describe, one whose event name","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"starts with ","type":"text"},{"code":"$","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", as Mixpanel’s own events’ names do, one with a property Mixpanel reads for itself","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(a ","type":"text"},{"code":"$","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"-prefixed one, ","type":"text"},{"code":"token","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"time","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"distinct_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"ip","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"bucket","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), one of 255 properties or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"more counting the encoder’s own, one holding an array of 255 elements or more, one whose property","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"nests objects more than 3 deep, one whose event isn’t","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"Encodable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", one holding a value JSON can’t, one whose timestamp is before 1971 or has no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"epoch-milliseconds form, and one too large for Mixpanel. The destination reports each as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"HTTPDropReport.skipped(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", a ","type":"text"},{"code":"SkippedRecord","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" whose reason is a ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelEncodingError"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Mixpanel answers 200 even when it ingests none of a request’s events, and its track API ingests"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"only events from the last 5 days, so a record older than that when it is sent is counted as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"delivered and not stored. A wrong region, or a token of no project, may be answered 200 with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"nothing stored too, so check the project’s Live View after setting the destination up."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"To send to PostHog or Amplitude, use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PostHogEncoding"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AmplitudeEncoding"},{"type":"text","text":" instead."}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["import HTTPDestinations","import MixpanelEncoding","import TrackingPlans","","let plan = try TrackingPlan()","let mixpanel = try HTTPDestination.mixpanel(","    projectToken: projectToken,","    region: .us,  \/\/ or .eu or .india, where the project's data resides","    plan: plan)","let tracker = Tracker(enrichers: [.sessions()])","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: mixpanel)"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The guide ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"covers what Mixpanel receives, and why, in more detail.","type":"text"}]}]}],"sections":[],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Framework","title":"MixpanelEncoding","modules":[{"name":"MixpanelEncoding"}],"role":"collection","externalID":"MixpanelEncoding","symbolKind":"module"},"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Sending-to-Mixpanel","identifiers":["doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/mixpanel(projectToken:region:plan:backoff:clock:)","doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/mixpanel(projectToken:region:plan:transport:backoff:clock:)","doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelRegion","doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelSetupError"],"title":"Sending to Mixpanel"},{"anchor":"Encoding-batches","identifiers":["doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelBatchEncoder"],"title":"Encoding batches"},{"anchor":"Records-left-out","identifiers":["doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelEncodingError"],"title":"Records left out"}],"references":{"doc://MixpanelEncoding/documentation/MixpanelEncoding/MixpanelBatchEncoder/batchLimit":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Mixpanel’s limits on one request: 2,000 events, 2,000,000 bytes of body, and 999,999 bytes"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of one event."}],"url":"\/documentation\/mixpanelencoding\/mixpanelbatchencoder\/batchlimit","type":"topic","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelBatchEncoder\/batchLimit","kind":"symbol","title":"batchLimit","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"batchLimit"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:12PropertyJSON10BatchLimitV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"BatchLimit"}]},"doc://MixpanelEncoding/documentation/MixpanelEncoding/MixpanelRegion":{"abstract":[{"text":"The data residency of a Mixpanel project, which decides the ","type":"text"},{"code":"\/track","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" endpoint its events are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"posted to.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/mixpanelencoding\/mixpanelregion","type":"topic","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelRegion","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MixpanelRegion"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"MixpanelRegion","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MixpanelRegion"}]},"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations":{"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations","type":"topic","role":"collection","abstract":[{"text":"Send each batch of records to an HTTP endpoint, and send it again until it arrives.","type":"text"}],"title":"HTTPDestinations","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations"},"doc://MixpanelEncoding/documentation/MixpanelEncoding/MixpanelEncodingError":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MixpanelEncodingError"}],"type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MixpanelEncodingError"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelEncodingError","url":"\/documentation\/mixpanelencoding\/mixpanelencodingerror","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Why "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelBatchEncoder"},{"type":"text","text":" couldn’t send a record, which it leaves out of the batch’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"requests as a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SkippedRecord"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" reports as a drop. When it can encode no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"record of a batch, it makes no request, and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" sends nothing for the batch."}],"kind":"symbol","title":"MixpanelEncodingError","role":"symbol"},"doc://MixpanelEncoding/documentation/MixpanelEncoding/HTTPDestinations/HTTPDestination/mixpanel(projectToken:region:plan:backoff:clock:)":{"role":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"A destination that sends batches to the Mixpanel project of ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"projectToken"},{"text":", whose data","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"resides in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"region"},{"text":", with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"URLSession.shared"},{"text":", retrying a send that fails for now with the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"waits of ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"backoff"},{"text":" on ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"clock"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/mixpanelencoding\/httpdestinations\/httpdestination\/mixpanel(projecttoken:region:plan:backoff:clock:)","conformance":{"conformancePrefix":[{"text":"Conforms when","type":"text"}],"availabilityPrefix":[{"text":"Available when","type":"text"}],"constraints":[{"code":"Transport","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"code":"URLSessionTransport","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"Encoding","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"code":"MixpanelBatchEncoder","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},"identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/mixpanel(projectToken:region:plan:backoff:clock:)","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"mixpanel"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"projectToken"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"region"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MixpanelRegion","preciseIdentifier":"s:16MixpanelEncoding0A6RegionO"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"plan"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"TrackingPlan","preciseIdentifier":"s:13TrackingPlans0A4PlanV"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"backoff"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"ExponentialBackoff","preciseIdentifier":"s:16HTTPDestinations18ExponentialBackoffV"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"clock"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"some"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Clock","preciseIdentifier":"s:12_Concurrency5ClockP"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Duration","preciseIdentifier":"s:s8DurationV"},{"kind":"text","text":">) "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MixpanelSetupError","preciseIdentifier":"s:16MixpanelEncoding0A10SetupErrorO"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"HTTPDestination","preciseIdentifier":"s:16HTTPDestinations15HTTPDestinationV"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"URLSessionTransport","preciseIdentifier":"s:16HTTPDestinations19URLSessionTransportV"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MixpanelBatchEncoder","preciseIdentifier":"s:16MixpanelEncoding0A12BatchEncoderV"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"title":"mixpanel(projectToken:region:plan:backoff:clock:)"},"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations/BatchEncoder":{"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"BatchEnco